  "burrow": {"enabled": false, "_why_r2": "close-1024 r1 CPU frame: at 40 m the mound sat inside the existing, larger faceted hill and did not show. r2: 64 m wide (about 22 m tall), centre 32 m back along the 315-degree axis so its tunnel mouth stays on the real mouth and its front covers the faceted front and slab ramp.", "_why": "F38 band2_stone_and_root_1 close-1024 (OFF until judged): the dominant object is the faceted Burrow mound with its slab ramp (GPU 5.82, P2-014 PRESENT). Coordinator Meshy burrow mound (tb/meshy-1024 ae67083ec): 40 m wide (about 14 m tall, 8x the 1.80 m trainer), its tunnel mouth at the real Warrens mouth (-357, 2610), centred 15 m back along the cave's 315-degree axis and facing the stand (yaw 135). Visual only; the real mouth, collision and route are unchanged.", "pieces": [{"id": "mound", "path": "res://assets/props/meshy-1024/meadows_burrow_mound/meadows_burrow_mound.glb", "at": [-379.6, 2632.6], "width_m": 64.0, "sink_m": 2.0, "yaw_deg": 135.0}]},
